{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"6867c0942e9c34bd","name":"card_unit_1st_london_brigade","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/WorldAtWar/units/card_unit_1st_london_brigade","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"1st LONDON BRIGADE","text":"Your other British ground units have +2 attack.","flavorText":"The 1st London Brigade was a formation of the British Territorial Army and saw service in WWI and WWII. From 1939 to 1943 the brigade remained in the UK, preparing for the expected German invasion, but in 1943 it was sent to Egypt. By then the formation had been renumbered to the 167th London Brigade and was now part of the 56th (London) Infantry Division which was under the command of the X Corps of the British Eighth Army. The brigade saw minimal service in the Tunisia Campaign and would after that participate in the Italian Campaign where it saw heavy fighting in numerous operations and battles, including the Battle of Anzio, the Battle of Salerno, and finally the Allied Spring 1945 offensive in Italy, codenamed Operation Grapeshot. The 167th London Brigade ended the war in Austria with the British Eighth Army.","faction":"Britain","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_1st_london_brigade","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_1st_london_brigade_title","SourceString":"1st LONDON BRIGADE","LocalizedString":"1st LONDON BRIGADE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":2,"defense":5,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_1st_london_brigade_text","SourceString":"Your other British ground units have +2 attack.","LocalizedString":"Your other British ground units have +2 attack."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_1st_london_brigade_history","SourceString":"The 1st London Brigade was a formation of the British Territorial Army and saw service in WWI and WWII. From 1939 to 1943 the brigade remained in the UK, preparing for the expected German invasion, but in 1943 it was sent to Egypt. By then the formation had been renumbered to the 167th London Brigade and was now part of the 56th (London) Infantry Division which was under the command of the X Corps of the British Eighth Army. The brigade saw minimal service in the Tunisia Campaign and would after that participate in the Italian Campaign where it saw heavy fighting in numerous operations and battles, including the Battle of Anzio, the Battle of Salerno, and finally the Allied Spring 1945 offensive in Italy, codenamed Operation Grapeshot. The 167th London Brigade ended the war in Austria with the British Eighth Army.","LocalizedString":"The 1st London Brigade was a formation of the British Territorial Army and saw service in WWI and WWII. From 1939 to 1943 the brigade remained in the UK, preparing for the expected German invasion, but in 1943 it was sent to Egypt. By then the formation had been renumbered to the 167th London Brigade and was now part of the 56th (London) Infantry Division which was under the command of the X Corps of the British Eighth Army. The brigade saw minimal service in the Tunisia Campaign and would after that participate in the Italian Campaign where it saw heavy fighting in numerous operations and battles, including the Battle of Anzio, the Battle of Salerno, and finally the Allied Spring 1945 offensive in Italy, codenamed Operation Grapeshot. The 167th London Brigade ended the war in Austria with the British Eighth Army."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WorldAtWar","showBoostIcon":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPlay","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardLeaveBoardOrOwner","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeOtherCardPlayedFromHand"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Guard"],"hasGuard":true,"soundBl